# 10. ROW LEVEL SECURITY (RLS)

Implement appropriate Supabase Row Level Security on all sensitive tables.

Security requirements:

## Students

Students can:

- View and update permitted fields of their own profile.
- View their own progress.
- View their own exam history.
- Save their own answers during authorized attempts.
- Submit their own exams.
- Access exams they are authorized to attempt.
- View their own results.

Students cannot:

- View other student records.
- Modify their own role.
- Approve themselves as teachers.
- Access admin data.
- Modify official scores directly.
- Modify other students' answers.
- Access teacher-only records.

## Teachers

Teachers can:

- Manage classes they own.
- Manage students enrolled in their classes, within permitted operations.
- Create and manage assignments they own.
- View results for their assigned students.
- Access teacher-specific analytics.

Teachers cannot:

- Access another teacher's private classes.
- Change their own role to admin.
- Approve their own teacher application.
- Access unrelated student data.
- Change official exam scores without an authorized workflow.

## Admin

Admin can access the administrative data necessary for platform management.

Admin privileges must be securely verified.

Do not implement admin security by checking only:

- A frontend variable
- localStorage
- A URL parameter
- A user-editable profile field

Use secure authorization mechanisms and trusted server-side checks.

Test RLS policies thoroughly.

